{{Quote|A sword that carries many burdens and lives, once used by an [[Saber Expert|expert of its kind]].|Item}}
The '''Saber''' is a {{Legendary}} [[sword]].

Known for its incredible damage, Saber V2 is still considered to be a fairly decent [[Swords|sword]] in [[PvP mechanics|PvP]] in the [[Second Sea]]. However, it is recommended that the player upgrades to a better sword as they progress out of the [[Second Sea]] and enter the [[Third Sea]], due to it's moves being near useless if the opponents use [[Instinct]].  

Despite it being a {{Legendary}} [[First Sea]] sword, because of the extremely slow M1’s, it's considered a horrible sword for late [[Second Sea]] and [[Third Sea]] as there are also other better choices of swords in those seas. 

==Obtainment==
===Version 1===
The Saber can be obtained by defeating the [[Saber Expert]] in completing the [[Saber/Puzzle|Saber puzzle]]. It has a 100% drop chance.

===Version 2===
The Saber can be [[Upgrading|upgraded]] to '''Saber V2''' by completing the following steps:
# Earn one million(1,000,000) [[Bounty and Honor System|Bounty/Honor]].
# Player must kill another player with a similar [[Levels|level]] (Or player under 25% around your level and it is irrespective of bounty/honor).
A message saying "Something weird has occurred to your <Saber>." will appear if done correctly. The names of the moves will not change, only the moves themselves.

If the player completes all the steps but doesn't have the Saber, a message saying "Something weird has happened, but you lack the required item".

;Notes
* The player killed does not need to have 1 Million [[Bounty and Honor System|Bounty/Honor]].
* Saber V1 will NOT change to Saber V2 if the kill was a suspicious kill.
* The player can get it in every sea as long as Bounty/Honor and level requirements are met.
* Saber V1 will NOT change to Saber V2 if the player killed was already killed 3/3 for the reward limit.

